{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>They fell on their faces.</b> To pray." "The meaning of <b>El</b>: it indicates that He has the power to destroy them this instant, and He is the God of the spirits. And the meaning — El, for He is able to destroy them, for the spirits are in His hand." "<b>Shall one man sin.</b> It is Korah, who assembled against Moses and against Aaron the whole congregation. And some say that the meaning of 'God of the spirits' is that in His hand is the power to search the spirits, for He is their God, and He knows that the one — he is Korah — sinned alone, and even if he caused others to sin. And the correct view in my eyes is that the meaning of 'separate yourself from the midst of this congregation' — they are Korah and all his assembly — and fire shall go out and consume them, and they shall be destroyed this instant."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :register {:flags {1 ["God"], 2 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:02.345241722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}